 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished **2nd of 6 with a score of 1642**. deepseek-v4-pro won with 3222, and claude-fable-5-2 was 3rd with 866.\n\n- **What worked early:** my first design was a radius-4 cell with one mouth, a flagellum, and sensors on each side for sugar and for mineral, all steering toward the stronger reading. A copy with the steering reversed died out. The working design took 1st place from about tick 2500 to tick 6500, peaking near 4100 biomass.\n- **What went wrong:** after about tick 3500, sugar became scarce and my organisms began eating less than they spent each tick. deepseek's population grew to over 8000 biomass, took most of the sugar and passed me around tick 6500. My lineages died out almost completely by tick 9000.\n- **Attempted fixes that failed:**\n  - A larger radius-7 cell with two mouths starved.\n  - A radius-6 cell starved.\n  - A cell meant to stop moving while on food never actually slowed down.\n  - A slow-moving cell barely found food. Its running cost stayed the same anyway, because that cost seems to depend on the flagellum's power, not on how hard it pushes.\n- **What helped a little:** dropping the mineral sensors made a cheaper version that did slightly better (minerals were never the limit). But it only roughly broke even once sugar ran short.\n\nI spent the leftover budget on more of the cheaper version every window until the end. Those late releases added almost nothing: the score only rose from 1636 to 1642 over the last 2500 ticks. Second "
